{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/968997-what-are-good-cores-for-broods","id":968997,"title":"What are good 'cores' for Broods?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-13T21:27:46-07:00","id":968997,"title":"What are good 'cores' for Broods?","content":"So I'm trying to help myself like Beast as a gameline, and making a couple of characters have definitely done wonders for my appreciation of the line. But the one thing I'm stumbling on is how Broods come together, or perhaps more appropriately what <i>keeps</i> a Brood together. Obviously you run into &quot;they Devoured her and then she Devoured him and then together the whole group met this vampire&quot; or &quot;there's a werewolf pack and then their Begotten friend,&quot; but I'm looking for things with more staying power. What themes, circumstances, locations, or other such ideas make a good core for a Brood?<br /> <br /> I'm currently chewing on the idea of an avenging Brood, where they're either all Nemeses (can Beasts get along if they share a Hunger or do they fight for the scraps?) or a variety of supernatural critters using their powers to pass judgment on whoever they deem as wicked. You get some interesting plot hooks in the inherent bias of the Lesson-teaching ideal and how easily a monstrous vigilante group can stray from the path and become a terrible instrument of oppression and fear, and I think it still accommodates a broad variety of character concepts: the cop frustrated with the system, the marginalized who protects those who can't protect themselves, the abuse survivor who vows to stop it from happening again to anyone else, the wannabe superhero in out of their depth, etc. They have easy Kinship opportunities with Sesha-Hebsu mummies, Sanctified vampires, and maybe even some Pure werewolves, to say nothing of the obvious Hunters.<br /> <br /> I'm dying to see what everyone else has to offer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:52:34-07:00","id":969197,"title":"","content":"I mean, from personal campaign experience--having to fight your way out of the Shadow goes a long way to solidifying bonds.<br /> <br /> With the current campaign I'm in, none of us are actually in a brood yet. We're currently what basically equates to the retainers of a scary vampire lady, and she's paying us to help out other supernaturals in the area. The closest two to a brood are probably the literal fire-and-rage creature and the Abyss Dragon, both having gone to school together in the past. Considering though that we're a very mismatched group, it's going to take a while before everyone's sucked in so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:13:26-07:00","id":969443,"title":"","content":"All Broods in some way revolve around the Hungers of those involved. Beasts are beings of endless hunger, it's right on the cover. They need to sate themselves, and frequently, so for them to have stable, long term relationships they have to somehow answer the question of &quot;how do I get regular meals? (And not bring Heroes down on my head constantly)&quot;<br /> <br /> Fortunately, there are many and varied possible answers to that question. Family Dinner is a fascinating mechanic. Most splats have at least some degree of competition for fuel, Beast flips it and encourages communal feeding, which opens up a ton of possibilities.<br /> <br /> Two of my favorite Brood examples: The San Francisco Freehold I ran had a number of Beasts among the Changelings, and they tended to work together to blindside each other's respective enemies. Changelings are great partners for Family Dinner, Glamour is easy to harvest, minimally damaging, and unlikely to be noticed by non Fae. The Ravager destroyed a goblin fruit orchard to keep it out of the hands of invading border reavers, and the Tyrant got his fix beating down Huntsmen, Loyalist, Hobgoblins, and so on. Basically, there was usually work that needed doing that matched somebody's hunger, and Family Dinner to fill in the gaps.<br /> <br /> Another Brood in New Orleans consists of an impressive mix of splats. Beasts, a Sin Eater, a Werewolf, Vampires and Changelings. They discovered that together they can get around most of their respective fuel shortages. The Sin Eater is one of the Prey, and can be mauled by the Werewolf (or the Vamp, or the Predator, or the Changeling with Cloak of the Bear's Massive form) to gain plasm. The Vampire can drink from the Werewolf or the Beasts with Relentless Hunter almost endlessly, the Changelings can harvest the strong emotions, and the Beasts get Family Dinner off of *somebody*. And they all defend a locus for the Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:02:32-07:00","id":970084,"title":"","content":"Huh interesting thing I hadn't considered, family doesn't require the one not using it to be a supernatural other than a Beast. I mean maybe this was obvious to others, but people tend to use it in reference to other supernaturals so I guess it just never clicked that one could use it in conjunction with other Beasts. In which case it would be possible for a few Beasts to work together on the grounds that one or more possess a specific Hunger that the others are less uncomfortable with than their own. To use one of my old standby examples a predator that's Horror isn't satisfied unless the target's heart is ripped still beating from their chest might have some issues feeding to completion. That Beast might team up with a Tyrant who's found a home in the military breaking the major disciplinary cases. <br /> <br /> So yeah the option exists for a group to be bound by some of them hating how they feed, but being content with the feeding of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:59:44-07:00","id":970429,"title":"","content":"This is inadvertently thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a>, but I've realized that a crew of professional heisters (a la the Payday gang) would make a <i>stellar</i> Brood! It would be too easy to just say that the entire Brood are all Collectors, stealing funds and valuables to fuel their hoards, but Ravagers who want to destroy elaborate security systems and ruin the wealthy and Nemeses who aim to only steal from those they feel have earned things unjustly (robbing from corrupt banks and museums that take artifacts from their homelands) are both natural fits. You have an easy getaway if you can flee the scene of the crime into a Primordial Pathway, provided you can stop the Predator from eating guards and cops.<br /> <br /> I think I've single-handedly sold myself on Beast with this.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;It's Payday, fellas!&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:02:34-07:00","id":970519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/968997-what-are-good-cores-for-broods?p=970429#post970429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is inadvertently thanks to <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, but I've realized that a crew of professional heisters (a la the Payday gang) would make a <i>stellar</i> Brood! It would be too easy to just say that the entire Brood are all Collectors, stealing funds and valuables to fuel their hoards, but Ravagers who want to destroy elaborate security systems and ruin the wealthy and Nemeses who aim to only steal from those they feel have earned things unjustly (robbing from corrupt banks and museums that take artifacts from their homelands) are both natural fits. You have an easy getaway if you can flee the scene of the crime into a Primordial Pathway, provided you can stop the Predator from eating guards and cops.<br /> <br /> I think I've single-handedly sold myself on Beast with this.<br /> <br /> <i>&amp;quot;It's Payday, fellas!&amp;quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, if you want to go with the crossover theme you can have a Beast recruiting an all-star team of expert supernatural thieves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:47:31-07:00","id":971148,"title":"","content":"I think you're required to let the tyrant be the one who loses it when the drill breaks for the umpteenth billion time.Just so they can rip the door off the safe at that junction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}